
## Images, Tags & Docker Hub

---

## 1. Go to Project

```bash
cd ~/devops-lab/docker-demo
```

Check files:

```bash
ls
```

Expected:

```text
app.py
Dockerfile
```

---

## 2. Build Image

```bash
docker build -t docker-demo:v1 .
```

Check images:

```bash
docker images
```

Image format:

```text
repository:tag

docker-demo:v1
```

---

## 3. Docker Tags

Create another tag:

```bash
docker tag docker-demo:v1 docker-demo:latest
```

List images:

```bash
docker images
```

Example:

```text
docker-demo    v1
docker-demo    latest
```

### Important

```text
Tag = Version/name given to an image

v1
v2
v3
latest
dev
production
```

`latest` does NOT automatically mean newest.

---

# 4. Docker Registry

A Docker registry stores Docker images.

Examples:

```text
Docker Hub
AWS ECR
GitHub Container Registry
```

Basic flow:

```text
Local Computer
      │
      │ docker push
      ▼
Docker Registry
      │
      │ docker pull
      ▼
Server
```

---

# 5. Docker Hub Login

```bash
docker login
```

After successful login:

```text
Login Succeeded
```

---

# 6. Tag Image for Docker Hub

Suppose your Docker Hub username is:

```text
YOUR_USERNAME
```

Tag:

```bash
docker tag docker-demo:v1 YOUR_USERNAME/docker-demo:v1
```

Image format:

```text
USERNAME/REPOSITORY:TAG
```

Example:

```text
gowtham123/docker-demo:v1
```

---

# 7. Push Image to Docker Hub

```bash
docker push YOUR_USERNAME/docker-demo:v1
```

Meaning:

```text
Local Image
     ↓
docker push
     ↓
Docker Hub
```

---

# 8. Pull Image from Docker Hub

```bash
docker pull YOUR_USERNAME/docker-demo:v1
```

Meaning:

```text
Docker Hub
     ↓
docker pull
     ↓
Local Computer
```

---

# 9. Run Image from Docker Hub

```bash
docker run -d \
  -p 8000:8000 \
  --name docker-demo-container \
  YOUR_USERNAME/docker-demo:v1
```

Test:

```bash
curl http://localhost:8000
```

Expected:

```text
Hello from Docker!
```

---

# 10. Docker Image History

See image layers/history:

```bash
docker history docker-demo:v1
```

Or:

```bash
docker history YOUR_USERNAME/docker-demo:v1
```

---

# 11. Inspect Image

```bash
docker image inspect docker-demo:v1
```

Shows detailed image information.

---

# ⭐ Important Commands

```bash
# Build image
docker build -t docker-demo:v1 .

# List images
docker images

# Create tag
docker tag docker-demo:v1 docker-demo:latest

# Login
docker login

# Tag for Docker Hub
docker tag docker-demo:v1 YOUR_USERNAME/docker-demo:v1

# Push image
docker push YOUR_USERNAME/docker-demo:v1

# Pull image
docker pull YOUR_USERNAME/docker-demo:v1

# Run image
docker run -d -p 8000:8000 \
  --name docker-demo-container \
  YOUR_USERNAME/docker-demo:v1

# Test application
curl http://localhost:8000

# Image history
docker history docker-demo:v1

# Image details
docker image inspect docker-demo:v1
```

